    {
      "id": "claim_17dd798408424a6897cfa4695b5d0547",
      "statement": "SQLiteStore calls db.SetMaxOpenConns(1) on its underlying connection pool to avoid \"database is locked\" errors on file-backed SQLite databases and to prevent an in-memory (:memory:) database from being split across multiple independent pool connections.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/sqlite.go#L48-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e694fb49f9bf240b2a9a3f8e58dae2d79da2effcc53f9eb1c0d6916a1ba66abc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6d33e0decab644d5b25c7870a6c9b441",
      "statement": "ClaimNextExecution atomically dequeues the oldest pending execution and transitions it to running: PostgresStore uses a transaction with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so concurrent workers each lock only the single row they claim and skip rows already locked by other in-flight claims; SQLiteStore relies on SetMaxOpenConns(1) serializing all connections process-wide to achieve the same safety, since SQLite has no FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED equivalent. Both order candidates by created_at ASC, id ASC and return store.ErrNotFound when no pending execution exists.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/postgres.go#L231-L274",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00a4edab11ba9e8625c4b218263b77bbca74255992db5b6578bbac4dc6505491:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/sqlite.go#L238-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69eee7c3f2d3759db544d7ffd6b9466b3bd27c399d3e99d55af9e19af2570586:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1ed98b1946b94d6ca49b38bbb03667e5",
      "statement": "UpdateExecutionWithResult transitions an execution to a terminal status and replaces its ExecutionOutput atomically inside a single transaction: it deletes any prior output row for the execution and inserts a new one only if output is non-nil, so retried or re-run executions never accumulate stale output rows; it returns ErrNotFound if no execution row was affected by the status update.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/postgres.go#L184-L229",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de9ae52362afe7ee86d99478c8d14842ac2a0a369f2b4c5d2ea1555f5205ad66:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/sqlite.go#L178-L236",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eef0b5c87f12c9039149620d111c09b1be6cade63aa15492c9c573fb4d53989a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_061eefef3d1c4c86875c6a3effacc3ed",
      "statement": "Execution lifecycle state is tracked only as the current status/approval_state columns on the executions row itself, with no separate execution-history table; this is distinct from the append-only, per-HTTP-request audit log written by middleware.NewAuditLogger via CreateAuditEntry, which records method/path/status/caller identity plus any handler-attached AuditContext fields for every request regardless of whether it touches an execution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/middleware/audit.go#L39-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7493744722dc66b7def6498320674530840f558ecca67d744894d25fd9cacc18:"
        },
        {
