          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c9e65fe3f6079d87263cdafd170595236d5cd4f8d2601d6ace471e389be2055:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d50000360c54c07b767caa9de22e41a",
      "statement": "Migrations are embedded per-dialect (migrations/sqlite and migrations/postgres) as paired up/down SQL files and tracked in a schema_migrations table; for Postgres, runMigrations acquires a session-level advisory lock (pg_advisory_lock, fixed key 0x526F7361) on a dedicated connection before applying migrations and releases it via a background context on return so replicas starting concurrently do not race, and so the unlock still runs if the caller's context was cancelled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/migrations.go#L16-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39bd49a26a5adbf64f57957c09d49f148343029297cebe2acf3c19f6667486ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5b4ed94963e340f280b5bb62ff1d1862",
      "statement": "RollbackLastMigration and rollbackMigration provide an explicit down-migration path: they look up the most recently applied schema_migrations version, execute its paired .down.sql file, and remove the schema_migrations row, all within one transaction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/migrations.go#L105-L150",
